WEBVTT

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:54.450
In my earliest memories,

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.450
my home was my entire world.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.220
My only acquaintance … was my owner.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.860
Then I met Ojisan, Takahiro, and Kokone,

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.910
and before I knew it, little by little,

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.710
my world was expanding.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.540
I stayed in Kamakura for two months.

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.630
I stayed and worked at a caféteria.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.780
It went okay for my first job.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.310
Is there a town down this way?

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:23.480
A town? There aren’t any that way.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.700
Is that so?

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:28.010
Ah, hold on for a bit.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:40.100
Here you go.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.730
Enoshima is now a deserted island.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:57.720
From there, I headed to the capital of the Kanagawa Nation as well.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.450
The road was long.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:12.890
So heavy …

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.670
Oh my! It’s delicious!

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:52.760
Before I set off on this trip,

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:57.350
I used to think that Asahina Pass bordered my hometown.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.440
But I don’t think so anymore.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:23.940
My world … keeps expanding.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.110
It’s as if my feelings evolve into colors,

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.370
and fade … into the sky.

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:58.540
There aren’t any hotels around here.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:03.160
What should I do?

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.690
I guess I could keep walking until morning.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:02.500
Oji-san—!

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:41.410
Um …

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.860
Is that so?

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:56.950
Bad timing, huh?

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.460
Um, thank you very much.

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:10.700
Well, I’ll be heading back then.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:11.880
Hey,

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:15.700
Alpha gave me her keys.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:18.600
How ’bout you stay here tonight?

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:20.780
But …

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.520
It’s already dark outside, and you’ll have to go through mountain roads.

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:26.790
So stay.

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:28.520
Okay.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.510
It’s the letter I sent.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:01.940
No wonder.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.870
Sorry for the intrusion …

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.440
Alpha …

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:38.960
I’m lost!

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:23.940
It’s so vast!

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:13.280
Can I help you?

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:17.690
Um, would you mind telling me where I am?

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:22.000
Why, this is Atsugi Airport.

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:25.980
Um, airport you say? Where planes land and take off?

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:29.440
Well, yeah. That’s what airports are usually for.

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:30.550
Then …

00:15:31.970 --> 00:15:33.930
Will I be able to see airplanes and stuff?

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:35.820
Well, yeah.

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:42.940
You’re a robot person, aren’t you?

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:44.230
Yes!

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:49.440
The pilot on that next flight is my kid; a robot too.

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:51.320
The next flight?

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:54.720
It should arrive in about an hour.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:56.490
Wanna wait?

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.080
Yes!

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:46.440
Hmm, it’s late.

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:00.850
Here it comes!

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:38.800
A customer?

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:40.990
No! Just looking around.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:43.350
It’s amazing.

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:46.960
You think so?

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:48.520
Yes! Absolutely!

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:53.450
Um, what is it?

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:57.440
Are you a robot too?

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.390
Seems you’re one as well.

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:04.600
Um …

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:06.850
Are you male?

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:09.310
Yeah, I suppose.

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.800
You’re a female, aren’t you?

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:15.770
Y-yeah.

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:17.410
I suppose.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:35.790
Excuse me!

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:41.680
Here. It’s dokudami tea.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.240
Ah, thanks!

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:51.880
Hey, Nye?

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:53.610
Hm?

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:55.720
Sorry about earlier.

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:57.280
Earlier?

00:18:57.670 --> 00:19:02.380
I always thought robots were all female, so …

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:05.300
I was surprised.

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:10.280
I’m used to it. I know a few robot people myself,

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:12.420
but I’ve never met a male one.

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:17.370
Does it make you curious?

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:22.200
To be honest, a little.

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:29.680
Male robots are weak, they say.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:33.630
I heard they all died early on.

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:38.450
I see.

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:50.060
Are you sleepy?

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:54.570
Thanks for letting me stay tonight.

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:57.420
I was sure I was gonna have to camp out.

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:01.150
Nye,

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:05.390
do you know any places hiring?

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:08.450
Nope.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:26.310
Makki, you know?

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:28.830
You’re heavy.

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:31.690
How rude!

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.420
You know, we haven’t seen Misago recently.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.290
Why’s she naked?

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:23.240
I dunno.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:27.410
Misago is … a robot person, isn’t she?

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:29.200
I dunno.

00:21:45.230 --> 00:21:46.180
You know?

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:49.960
I want to go to Enoshima,
or someplace, in the near future.

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:52.990
Don’t be silly. That’s far away.

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:55.270
I don’t mind if it is.

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:57.320
You can’t get there with a scooter.

00:21:57.940 --> 00:21:59.760
We could borrow a car from someone.

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:00.820
Who’s gonna drive?

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:03.170
We can learn.

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:05.950
Oh, you …

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:10.430
It’ll be all right.

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:17.460
I wonder …

00:23:18.680 --> 00:23:20.420
Where you are now?

00:23:23.020 --> 00:23:26.750
But, by the time you read this letter,

00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:32.480
you’d be back home, right? Alpha?

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:40.500
When you come back, I’ll be sure to …

00:23:58.440 --> 00:23:59.490
It’s Mount Fuji.

00:24:03.260 --> 00:24:06.160
I liked how it looked back when it was whole too.

00:24:07.650 --> 00:24:13.600
But I prefer the relaxed shape of this Mount Fuji.

00:25:09.100 --> 00:25:10.930
I’d like one!

00:25:12.420 --> 00:25:14.610
Y-y-yes!

00:25:20.260 --> 00:25:23.900
Just one moment please. It’ll be ready soon.

00:25:41.930 --> 00:25:42.960
This area …

00:25:43.910 --> 00:25:44.920
You know?

00:25:45.420 --> 00:25:46.080
Yes?

00:25:53.170 --> 00:25:55.530
It’s good for the eyes, isn’t it?

00:25:55.950 --> 00:25:57.170
It sure is.

00:26:04.650 --> 00:26:06.600
Here! Thanks for waiting!

00:26:14.550 --> 00:26:15.940
Thank you very much!

00:32:12.400 --> 00:32:13.350
All right!

00:32:17.740 --> 00:32:18.730
Time go back …

00:32:21.410 --> 00:32:23.610
Yes … Back to my home!
